# 必考词 Unit17
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit17核心高频词汇

{{practical}}{/ˈpræktɪkl/}}{adj. 实际的；实用的}}{{The course provides practical skills for the workplace.}}

{{pray}}{/preɪ/}}{v. 祈祷；请求}}{{The villagers prayed for rain during the drought.}}

{{precede}}{/prɪˈsiːd/}}{v. 在...之前；先于}}{{A brief introduction preceded the main lecture.}}

{{precious}}{/ˈpreʃəs/}}{adj. 珍贵的；宝贵的}}{{Clean water is a precious resource in many regions.}}

{{precise}}{/prɪˈsaɪs/}}{adj. 精确的；准确的}}{{Please give me the precise time of the meeting.}}

{{predict}}{/prɪˈdɪkt/}}{v. 预言；预测}}{{It is difficult to predict the outcome of the negotiations.}}

{{dominant}}{/ˈdɒmɪnənt/}}{adj. 支配的；占优势的}}{{English is the dominant language in international business.}}

{{prejudice}}{/ˈpredʒudɪs/}}{n. 偏见；歧视}}{{Prejudice against minority groups remains a serious problem.}}

{{preliminary}}{/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri/}}{adj. 初步的；预备的}}{{The preliminary results are encouraging.}}

{{premise}}{/ˈpremɪs/}}{n. 前提；假设}}{{The argument is based on a false premise.}}

{{preserve}}{/prɪˈzɜːrv/}}{v. 保护；保存}}{{It is our duty to preserve the environment for future generations.}}

{{press}}{/pres/}}{v. 按；催促；n. 新闻界}}{{The press reported the story extensively.}}

{{prestige}}{/preˈstiːʒ/}}{n. 威望；声望}}{{The university enjoys international prestige.}}

{{presume}}{/prɪˈzjuːm/}}{v. 假定；认为}}{{I presume you have already read the instructions.}}

{{previous}}{/ˈpriːviəs/}}{adj. 先前的；以前的}}{{She had no previous experience in management.}}

{{primary}}{/ˈpraɪməri/}}{adj. 主要的；初级的}}{{The primary goal of the project is to improve education.}}

{{prime}}{/praɪm/}}{adj. 主要的；n. 全盛期}}{{The prime minister gave a speech on national television.}}

{{principle}}{/ˈprɪnsəpl/}}{n. 原则；原理}}{{The company operates on the principle of fairness.}}

{{prior}}{/ˈpraɪər/}}{adj. 在前的；优先的}}{{Prior to the meeting, please review the documents.}}

{{priority}}{/praɪˈɒrəti/}}{n. 优先事项；重点}}{{Safety should always be the top priority.}}

{{privilege}}{/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ/}}{n. 特权；荣幸}}{{Education is a right, not a privilege.}}

{{probe}}{/prəʊb/}}{v. 探查；n. 探测器}}{{Scientists sent a space probe to explore Mars.}}

{{proceed}}{/prəˈsiːd/}}{v. 继续进行；前进}}{{After the break, the meeting proceeded as planned.}}

{{process}}{/ˈprəʊses/}}{n. 过程；v. 处理}}{{Learning a language is a long and gradual process.}}

{{produce}}{/prəˈdjuːs/}}{v. 生产；产生}}{{The factory produces high-quality electronic devices.}}

{{profession}}{/prəˈfeʃn/}}{n. 职业；行业}}{{Medicine is a highly respected profession.}}

{{profit}}{/ˈprɒfɪt/}}{n. 利润；v. 获益}}{{The company reported record profits this quarter.}}

{{profound}}{/prəˈfaʊnd/}}{adj. 深刻的；深远的}}{{The book had a profound impact on her thinking.}}

{{progress}}{/ˈprəʊɡres/}}{n./v. 进步；进展}}{{Significant progress has been made in cancer research.}}

{{prohibit}}{/prəˈhɪbɪt/}}{v. 禁止；阻止}}{{The law prohibits the sale of alcohol to minors.}}

{{project}}{/ˈprɒdʒekt/}}{n. 项目；计划}}{{The construction project will take two years to complete.}}

{{prominent}}{/ˈprɒmɪnənt/}}{adj. 突出的；著名的}}{{He is a prominent figure in the field of economics.}}

{{promote}}{/prəˈməʊt/}}{v. 促进；提升；推广}}{{The company promotes a healthy work-life balance.}}

{{prompt}}{/prɒmpt/}}{adj. 迅速的；v. 促使}}{{The crisis prompted the government to take immediate action.}}

{{proof}}{/pruːf/}}{n. 证据；证明}}{{There is no proof that the theory is correct.}}

{{proportion}}{/prəˈpɔːrʃn/}}{n. 比例；部分}}{{A large proportion of the population lives in cities.}}

{{propose}}{/prəˈpəʊz/}}{v. 提议；建议}}{{She proposed a new plan to improve efficiency.}}

{{prospect}}{/ˈprɒspekt/}}{n. 前景；可能性}}{{The prospects for economic growth look promising.}}

{{prosperity}}{/prɒˈsperəti/}}{n. 繁荣；兴旺}}{{The country enjoyed a period of peace and prosperity.}}

{{protest}}{/prəˈtest/}}{v./n. 抗议；反对}}{{Thousands of people protested against the new law.}}
